# Copy this file to .dev.vars for local Wrangler development.
# This placeholder is intentionally non-secret. Use Cloudflare's managed secret
# storage for staging and production values.
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA

# Abuse-control identifiers require a separate, unique 32-byte HMAC key encoded
# as canonical unpadded base64url. Keep the previous key for at least 24 hours
# during rotation so exact rolling IP quotas overlap without storing raw IPs.
# ABUSE_IP_HMAC_KEY=<32 random bytes as unpadded base64url>
# ABUSE_IP_HMAC_PREVIOUS_KEY=<previous key during a 24-hour overlap>

# Secret creation also requires SECRET_PREPARATION_HMAC_KEY. Generate a unique
# canonical unpadded base64url value from exactly 32 random bytes and store it
# only in the ignored .dev.vars file. No signing-key placeholder is committed.
# SECRET_PREPARATION_HMAC_PREVIOUS_KEY is optional and verification-only during
# a bounded rotation grace period; never reuse a checked-in placeholder for it.

# Administrative trust stays absent/unavailable by default. Configure only under
# a separately authorized operational change; never commit operator identities.
# ADMIN_ACCESS_ISSUER=<exact reviewed HTTPS Access team origin>
# ADMIN_ACCESS_AUDIENCE=<exact reviewed application audience>
# ADMIN_OPERATOR_EMAILS=<JSON array of exact approved operator email strings>
# Local automated fixtures use an isolated .invalid issuer and synthetic keys.
